@startuml
title Rios Vivos — asynchronous ingestion and answer workflow
autonumber

actor User
participant "Web/Admin client" as Client
participant "system-api" as API
database "PostgreSQL\nACL + job state" as DB
queue "Durable queue" as Queue
participant "AI-host worker" as Worker
database "Source storage\nS3 or encrypted disk" as Store
database "Vector index" as Index
participant "Local model" as Model
participant "WebSocket" as WS

== Ingest a document version ==
User -> Client : choose file
Client -> API : upload / request ingestion
API -> DB : validate ownership, visibility, version
API -> Store : save immutable source version
API -> DB : create job(queued)
API -> Queue : enqueue(document-id:version:checksum)
API --> Client : 202 + jobId
API -> WS : queued
WS --> Client : progress event
Worker -> Queue : reserve job
Worker -> DB : state: extracting / chunking / embedding
Worker -> Store : read source
Worker -> Index : upsert chunks with document/version IDs
Worker -> DB : indexed + audit
Worker -> WS : completed
WS --> Client : completed + version

== Ask a question ==
User -> Client : ask question
Client -> API : create RAG query
API -> DB : authenticate; derive allowed document versions
alt no authorized sources
  API -> DB : result(not-supported or denied)
  API --> Client : terminal result
else allowed sources
  API -> DB : create query job(queued)
  API -> Queue : enqueue(query job + ACL scope)
  API --> Client : 202 + jobId
  Worker -> Queue : reserve job
  Worker -> Index : retrieve only allowed versions
  Worker -> Model : question + retrieved passages
  Model --> Worker : answer + cited chunks or not-supported
  Worker -> DB : result, citations, model versions, audit
  Worker -> WS : completed
  WS --> Client : answer + citations
end

note over Client,WS
Polling the persisted job record is the fallback after
disconnects; WebSocket events alone are never authoritative.
end note
@enduml
